                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use a common base and factor the quadratic in ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\log_2(x)",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", retaining the zero root.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "The domain is $x>0$. Let $t=\\log_2(x)$. By change of base, $\\log_3(x)=\\frac{t}{\\log_2(3)}$ and $\\log_4(x)=\\frac{t}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{t^2}{\\log_2(3)}&=\\frac{t}{2}\\\\t^2&=\\frac{\\log_2(3)}{2}t\\\\t\\left(t-\\frac{\\log_2(3)}{2}\\right)&=0\\\\t&=0\\text{ or }\\frac{\\log_2(3)}{2}\\\\x&=2^0\\text{ or }2^{\\frac{1}{2}\\log_2(3)}\\\\x&=1\\text{ or }\\sqrt{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are positive and satisfy the original equation.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
